@startuml
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
autonumber

title Figure 4-1. Design Sequence: Get Journey State

actor "Traveler" as User
participant "Dashboard UI\n(Vue 3 + TypeScript)" as UI
participant "JourneyHandler\n(Gin)" as API
participant "Runtime" as RT
participant "MemoryStore" as Store
participant "SSEHub" as Hub

User -> UI : open or refresh the journey page
activate UI
UI -> API : GET /api/v1/journey/{id}/state
activate API
API -> RT : GetSnapshot(id)
activate RT
RT -> Store : GetSnapshot(id)
Store --> RT : JourneySnapshot (status = processing | ready | failed)
RT --> API : JourneySnapshot
deactivate RT
API --> UI : 200 OK + JourneySnapshot
deactivate API

alt status = processing
  UI --> User : skeleton screen (no risk colour, no action cards)
else status = ready
  UI --> User : render flight status, timeline, risk level, cards and actions
else status = failed
  UI --> User : keep last ready content, show error and retry entry
end

group real-time updates (Server-Sent Events)
  UI -> API : GET /api/v1/journey/{id}/stream
  activate API
  API -> RT : Subscribe(id)
  RT -> Hub : Subscribe(id)
  Hub --> RT : snapshot channel
  RT --> API : snapshot channel + current snapshot
  API --> UI : event: snapshot (full JourneySnapshot)
  loop no change for 15 s
    API --> UI : event: heartbeat
  end
  note over UI
    EventSource reconnects automatically;
    if the stream stays down for more than 20 s,
    the UI falls back to polling /state every 15 s.
  end note
  deactivate API
end
deactivate UI

note over RT
  Recalculation runs asynchronously: it is triggered by
  POST /journey, POST /journey/{id}/location, or the periodic
  scheduler (15 s tick, at most once per journey every 2 min).
  Results are published as full snapshots through SSEHub.
end note

note over Store
  Snapshots are keyed by journey.id and replaced as a whole.
  GET /state never triggers recalculation.
end note

@enduml
